WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:09.600
Another great way of getting data in data science&nbsp;
is by scraping data. This is important because not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:15.760
all data comes in nice JSON formats. Not all&nbsp;
data is built for access and so sometimes you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:22.000
have to get creative in how you access the data.&nbsp;
For instance, I can include HTML text on a web&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:28.480
page or tables on Wikipedia or PDF documents or&nbsp;
media like images and video and audio and so on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:33.760
Also, there's Word documents and there's&nbsp;
PowerPoint presentations, and any number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.560
of sources that have data that do not come in&nbsp;
a nice package for importing into Python or R.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.960
Be aware of issues of copyright and&nbsp;
confidentiality. This data was not created&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.160
for you to scrape and sometimes there are reasons&nbsp;
why it's been restricted. You need to be aware&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:55.440
of what the restrictions are and to respect those&nbsp;
and operate professionally. If you want to scrape&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:03.920
data, you have a couple of choices. One is use&nbsp;
readymade tools. For instance, import.io. That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:09.200
both a web address and it's the name of a tool&nbsp;
that makes scraping data from web pages very easy.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:16.240
ScraperWiki and Tabula also make this easy.&nbsp;
In fact, in Google Sheets you can simply use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:21.840
the =IMPORTHTML_ command to pull data out of&nbsp;
a table and even some versions of Excel make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:29.840
this possible. Or, you can use custom tools. You&nbsp;
can scrape data through R, Python, Java, or PHP.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:34.640
Any of these will make it possible for&nbsp;
you to access data and manipulate it in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.600
the ways that you need to get&nbsp;
it in to an analyzable format.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:43.360
In conclusion, scraping works when APIs don't&nbsp;
exist for the data that you want to work with.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:48.480
Also, you can use specialized apps that&nbsp;
were created for scraping or you can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:54.160
code in your language of choice. Finally,&nbsp;
copyright and confidentiality issues matter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.160 --> 00:02:01.920
and they should always be considered carefully&nbsp;
before you start scraping data off the web.

